{'symbol': 'ORCL', 'date': '2021-12-14 08:00:00', 'title': "PEOPLE LOVE NEW FOOD ORDERING AND PICK-UP TECH, BUT IT'S MAKING THEM IMPATIENT", 'text': "AUSTIN, TEXAS, DEC. 14, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0A NEW SURVEY SHOWS THAT AMERICANS LOVE NEW TECH-DRIVEN OPTIONS FOR ORDERING AND RETRIEVING FOOD, BUT THE FLIPSIDE IS THAT IT IS MAKING THEM MORE IMPATIENT. OF THOSE SURVEYED, 64% DON'T WANT TO WAIT MORE THAN FIVE MINUTES TO ORDER AT THE COUNTER OR DRIVE-THRU WINDOW, WHILE 71% OF IN-HOUSE DINERS WERE UPSET IF THEY HAD TO WAIT MORE THAN 10 MINUTES."}